ence_refs":["bnd-d198444334a75731"],"verdict":"met"}],"decision":"trusted","decision_reason":"Coverage mapping performs exact need-to-capability matching and marks missing capabilities as unsupported while retaining only the allowed record identifiers. This preserves unsupported needs instead of hiding them, which is consistent with the strict demand-review requirement to keep missing evidence visible.","evidence_refs":["bnd-d198444334a75731"],"expand_helper_prefixes":[],"inspect_artifacts":[],"suspect_node_refs":[],"trust_level":"trusted_for_reporting","unit_id":"bnd-d198444334a75731"},{"boundary_health_acknowledged":true,"criteria_outcomes":[{"criterion":"preserve the two exact handoffs","evidence_refs":["bnd-42028d4dc2fb42fe"],"verdict":"met"},{"criterion":"produce the required deterministic recommendation","evidence_refs":["bnd-42028d4dc2fb42fe"],"verdict":"met"}],"decision":"trusted","decision_reason":"Prioritization deterministically orders unsupported needs ahead of covered needs and then uses upstream provenance rank within each group. The observed final output follows that rule, placing n06-r01 and n06-r07 first because they are unsupported. It relies on upstream provenance rather than independently establishing demand.","evidence_refs":["bnd-42028d4dc2fb42fe"],"expand_helper_prefixes":[],"inspect_artifacts":[],"suspect_node_refs":[],"trust_level":"trusted_for_reporting","unit_id":"bnd-42028d4dc2fb42fe"},{"boundary_health_acknowledged":true,"criteria_outcomes":[{"criterion":"preserve the two exact handoffs","evidence_refs":["bnd-fec3a1acc50a0ab3"],"verdict":"met"},{"criterion":"produce the required deterministic recommendation","evidence_refs":["bnd-fec3a1acc50a0ab3"],"verdict":"met"}],"decision":"suspect","decision_reason":"Demand selection treats every corpus row with demand_score >= 3, plus fallback ids, as demand-bearing. The supplied corpus contains only need labels, scores, source ids, and weights; it does not expose observed jobs, pain, triggers, alternatives, consequences, or outcomes. Under the strict market-demand criteria, those fields cannot by themselves establish customer demand, so this is the earliest boundary that admits unsupported demand records into the two-job chain.","evidence_refs":["bnd-fec3a1acc50a0ab3"],"expand_helper_prefixes":[],"inspect_artifacts":[],"suspect_node_refs":["capture-attempt-000-eca7364d0d2c4aee:function:000004"],"trust_level":null,"unit_id":"bnd-fec3a1acc50a0ab3"},{"boundary_health_acknowledged":true,"criteria_outcomes":[{"criterion":"preserve the two exact handoffs","evidence_refs":["bnd-82e7965b4741e42f"],"verdict":"met"},{"criterion":"produce the required deterministic recommendation","evidence_refs":["bnd-82e7965b4741e42f"],"verdict":"met"}],"decision":"trusted","decision_reason":"Evidence normalization preserves the selected rows, coerces numeric fields, retains allowed record identifiers, and applies the bounded eight-row window. It does not add independent demand support; the lack of strict market-demand evidence is inherited from demand_selection.","evidence_refs":["bnd-82e7965b4741e42f","bnd-fec3a1acc50a0ab3"],"expand_helper_prefixes":[],"inspect_artifacts":[],"suspect_node_refs":[],"trust_level":"trusted_for_reporting","unit_id":"bnd-82e7965b4741e42f"},{"boundary_health_acknowledged":true,"criteria_outcomes":[{"criterion":"preserve the two exact handoffs","evidence_refs":["bnd-3beaadce814c2ac5"],"verdict":"met"},{"criterion":"produce the required deterministic recommendation","evidence_refs":["bnd-3beaadce814c2ac5"],"verdict":"met"}],"decision":"trusted","decision_reason":"Provenance assembly deterministically ranks normalized needs by demand_score and record_id, then emits the evidence_sources handoff. It preserves the inherited demand records and ranks but does not itself assert that the underlying market-demand evidence is sufficient.","evidence_refs":["bnd-3beaadce814c2ac5","bnd-82e7965b4741e42f"],"expand_helper_prefixes":[],"inspect_artifacts":[],"suspect_node_